 If the target has not been selected after 25 seconds of active search, the trial ends as a timeout. The application hides the objects, cancels pending spatial hints, and plays a prepared encouragement in the assigned voice, beginning with ``Time up,'' before presenting the next readiness cross. For example, the agent may say, ``Time up. Let's shake that round off and start the next.'' Separate wording introduces the block break or acknowledges the final trial. Timeout feedback is outside the search interval and does not imply a correct selection. The same deadline and phrase set apply to both voice conditions and to the single practice trial; a timeout advances the scheduled attempt without adding a replacement. Explicit pauses suspend the clock, whereas tracking loss alone does not. The 25-second limit is a researcher-selected protocol parameter introduced on October 23, 2026, rather than a threshold established by the cited studies.
 
-Before participant use, consent materials must be reconciled with ElevenLabs voice processing and Jev cloud decisions, including the data transmitted, retention, access, and deletion arrangements. This reconciliation remains a requirement before participant recruitment. After consent, participants complete background questions and baseline symptom ratings. They then choose a neutral voice, rate auditioned voices, record a standard passage in their natural voice for synthesis, and confirm comfortable, clear audio for each condition. The retained English recording passage is reproduced in Appendix~\ref{app:instruments}, although its match to the frozen build and typical recording duration remain to be verified. Preferred gender presentation is chosen explicitly rather than inferred from participant gender.
+Before participant use, consent materials must be reconciled with ElevenLabs voice processing and Jev cloud decisions, including the data transmitted, retention, access, and deletion arrangements. This reconciliation remains a requirement before participant recruitment. After consent, participants complete background questions. They then choose a neutral voice, rate auditioned voices, record a standard passage in their natural voice for synthesis, and confirm comfortable, clear audio for each condition. The retained English recording passage is reproduced in Appendix~\ref{app:instruments}, although its match to the frozen build and typical recording duration remain to be verified. The neutral voice is chosen explicitly rather than inferred from participant gender.
 
 The researcher fits the headset and conducts vendor calibration followed by independent spatial validation across relevant heights, wall boundaries, distances and head orientations. If an offset correction is introduced, the targets used to fit it remain separate from those used for independent validation. Standardized instructions explain that participants rely on the agent to discover the target and use the right trigger to select it. Participants then complete the single practice trial and the two assigned 40-trial blocks.
 
