 \section{Retrospective Questionnaires and Burden}
 The final-only survey avoids interrupting the two-block search sequence with a long questionnaire, but it also requires participants to recall Block 1 after completing Block 2. Ratings may therefore reflect recency, contrast, or imperfect recall. Each rating set identifies its referenced block; the reminder linking that block to its voice remains to be piloted. These reminders may aid recall but cannot guarantee accurate recollection.
 
-The condition-specific battery contains 130 numeric responses across both blocks, in addition to symptoms, setup ratings, comparison questions, and debrief. Its completion time, missingness, and comprehension therefore require pilot measurement. Because participants may be tired or symptomatic after exposure, the post-exposure safety check precedes the retrospective sets. The breadth of the battery reflects a current design decision; it does not demonstrate that every item is necessary or equally interpretable.
+The condition-specific battery contains 130 numeric responses across both blocks, in addition to setup ratings, comparison questions, and debrief. Its completion time, missingness, and comprehension therefore require pilot measurement. Because participants may be tired or uncomfortable after exposure, researchers check whether they are comfortable continuing before administering the retrospective sets. The breadth of the battery reflects a current design decision; it does not demonstrate that every item is necessary or equally interpretable.
 
 Adapting an embodied-agent measure to a voice agent can alter its meaning. Co-presence or anthropomorphism items may be understood differently without a visible character. The thesis retains attribution and wording changes, reports the adaptation, and avoids asserting new psychometric validation from a small experimental sample. Custom reliance and naturalness items remain individual exploratory measures.
 
